.TH RTDO 1 "September 2026" "unix-core" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rtdo \- Root Do: secure privilege executor with password authentication restricted to wheel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rtdo
.I command
[\fIarguments\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rtdo
is a secure, minimalist, POSIX-compliant privilege elevation utility designed as a lightweight alternative to
.BR sudo (8)
and
.BR doas (1).
Execution is strictly restricted to members of the
.B wheel
administrative group.
.PP
When invoked,
.B rtdo
verifies that the caller belongs to the
.B wheel
group (or is root), prompts for the caller's password directly on the controlling terminal (\fI/dev/tty\fR) with echo disabled, validates the password against the system shadow database, cleanses the execution environment, drops supplementary groups, assumes root credentials, and executes the specified command via
.BR execvp (3).
.PP
If the terminal input is interrupted (e.g. with \fBSIGINT\fR or \fBSIGQUIT\fR), terminal echo attributes are cleanly restored before exit.
.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.IP \(bu 2
.B Group Restriction:
The binary permissions must be set to \fIchmod 4750\fR owned by \fIroot:wheel\fR. In addition, an internal runtime verification ensures only members of group \fIwheel\fR can execute it.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Memory Sanitization:
Passwords in memory are immediately cleared using
.BR explicit_bzero (3)
after cryptographic comparison.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Environment Sanitization:
Dangerous variables such as \fBLD_PRELOAD\fR, \fBLD_LIBRARY_PATH\fR, and \fBIFS\fR are stripped, and a secure \fBPATH\fR is enforced if unset.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion of the executed command.
.TP
.B 1
Authentication failure, access denied, or invalid arguments.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by user signal (\fBSIGINT\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rtgo (1),
.BR doas (1),
.BR sudo (8),
.BR crypt (3)
